I developed an AI-powered drone-based traffic monitoring system using Machine Learning and Python to improve road safety and automate traffic rule enforcement in the UAE.

🚁 System Highlights
Live Video & GPS Tracking: Real-time feed via Raspberry Pi 5 with GPS integration.
Vehicle & License Plate Detection: YOLOv8 + EasyOCR to detect vehicles and recognize license plates.
Speed Monitoring & Violation Detection: GPS-based speed estimation; vehicles exceeding 120 km/h flagged automatically.
Automated Violation Reporting: Email alerts with plate number + video evidence; large files auto-uploaded to Google Drive.
Video Recording & Snippets: Full recordings (AVI) plus 10s violation clips (H.264).
Real-Time Overlays: On-screen display of speed, license plates, and violation highlights (green = safe, red = violation).
Error Handling & Logging: Auto-recovery from camera/GPS failures with detailed logs for debugging.
⚡ Tech Stack: Python, OpenCV, YOLOv8, EasyOCR, libcamera, SMTP, Google Drive API, Raspberry Pi 5, GPS modules.

🔹 Machine Learning Models Applied
YOLOv8: Object detection for vehicles in live drone video.
EasyOCR: High-accuracy license plate recognition.
GPS + Haversine Formula: Speed calculation and violation detection.

🔹 Python Development Work
Built an end-to-end ML pipeline for video capture, GPS data processing, and real-time inference.
Developed overlay features showing speed, license plates, and violations.
Implemented automated email notifications with attachments or cloud links.
Added robust error handling and logging for fault tolerance.
Optimized system for Raspberry Pi 5 deployment with efficient video handling and threaded processing.
✅ Impact:
This solution delivers real-time, AI-powered traffic monitoring that reduces manual enforcement, improves road safety, and establishes a scalable foundation for smart city infrastructure.
